HR Employee Attrition Analysis | Power BI & Python

Project Overview

This project focuses on analyzing employee attrition to identify workforce trends, understand potential factors contributing to employee turnover, and provide actionable insights to support data-driven HR decisions.

The analysis was conducted using a dataset containing 1,470 employee records.

Objectives

- Analyze overall employee attrition and workforce trends.
- Identify departments and job roles with higher attrition rates.
- Explore the relationship between overtime and employee turnover.
- Detect and investigate potential outliers.
- Develop actionable recommendations to support employee retention.

Tools & Technologies

- Power BI: Interactive dashboard and data visualization.
- DAX: KPI calculations and analytical measures.
- Python: Data analysis and outlier detection.
- Pandas: Data manipulation and analysis.
- Excel: Initial data exploration.

Key Findings

- Overall attrition rate: 16.12%.
- Employees working overtime showed a higher attrition rate.
- Attrition rates varied across departments and job roles.
- Potential outliers were identified using the IQR method and reviewed based on business context rather than automatically removed.

Deliverables

- Interactive Power BI dashboard.
- Python analysis and outlier detection.
- Key business insights and actionable recommendations.

Business Recommendations

- Investigate high-attrition job roles.
- Review workload and overtime practices.
- Strengthen employee engagement and retention initiatives.
- Monitor HR KPIs regularly to identify emerging trends.

Key Takeaway

This project demonstrates how data analytics and visualization can transform raw HR data into meaningful business insights and practical recommendations.

